# TypeScript and React Conventions

- Use explicit, narrow types for props, return values, and API payloads.
- Avoid `any`; prefer `unknown` + narrowing when type certainty is not immediate.
- Keep hooks at top level and move reusable async/data logic into custom hooks.
- Keep components focused: view rendering in components, logic in helpers/hooks.
- Prefer existing path alias imports (`@/...`) where they improve readability.
- Match existing naming and file-local formatting conventions in the touched module.
